        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add shareable subscription usage cards",
        "body": "## What this adds\n\nCodexBar already makes subscription usage visible in the menu bar, but those stats are difficult to copy, screenshot, or share. This PR adds a native **Share Stats…** action that opens a polished, fixed-size usage card designed for social sharing.\n\n- Shows every enabled/configured AI subscription in one 1200×630 card\n- Leads with combined 30-day tracked tokens and estimated spend\n- Separates a ranked **By subscription** list from a ranked **Top models** list\n- Builds model rankings from real local daily `modelBreakdowns`, with the provider shown under each model\n- Uses the existing CodexBar palette to keep subscriptions and their models visually distinct\n- Provides **Copy Image**, **Copy Stats**, and **Save…** actions from a local preview window\n- Exposes the same local preview from Settings → Menu → Sharing\n- Keeps the export privacy-safe: no account identity, email, project path, prompt content, or network upload\n\nProviders without priced local history remain visible as connected subscriptions; they are never reported as zero spend. The card uses explicit provenance language (`tracked`, `estimated`, `generated locally`) throughout.\n\n## Why\n\nUsage is increasingly part of how people compare and talk about AI tooling. A share surface turns CodexBar's existing multi-provider view into a useful artifact without adding an account system or hosted backend.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] `swift build`\n- [x] `swift test --filter ShareStatsTests` — 3 tests pass\n- [x] `make check` — passes; only the repository's existing locale catalog warnings remain\n- [x] Generated and visually inspected a real four-subscription card with current model breakdowns\n- [x] Verified the exported 1200×630 PNG is accepted by the macOS pasteboard\n- [ ] Full sharded suite in CI\n\n`Scripts/package_app.sh` completed the main Release build but the optional widget extension step is blocked on this machine by an Xcode `IDESimulatorFoundation` / `DVTDownloads` plugin-version mismatch. A no-widget app bundle was packaged and launched successfully, so this is noted as a local toolchain limitation rather than hidden as a code failure.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR intentionally contains only the share-card workflow. The unified Settings usage/spend dashboard is isolated in #2116.\n\n## Design sign-off\n\n`VISION.md` classifies new features as requiring sign-off. This draft is intentionally requesting maintainer feedback on the product surface, export contents, and privacy/provenance language before it is marked ready for review.\n",
